body:
**suggestion (bug_risk):** Excerpt generation always appends ellipsis and doesn’t guard against missing `html_content`.

This calls `post.html_content.replace(...).substring(0, 150)` unconditionally and always appends `...`. If `html_content` is `null`/`undefined`, this will throw, and when the content is shorter than 150 chars you still show an ellipsis even though nothing was truncated. Please guard against falsy `html_content` and only append the ellipsis when the text actually exceeds the limit.

```suggestion
                  <CardContent className="flex-grow">
                    <p className="text-slate-400/90 line-clamp-3 leading-relaxed font-light text-[15px]">
                      {(() => {
                        const rawHtml = post.html_content ?? '';
                        const plainText = rawHtml
                          .replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '')
                          .trim();
                        const limit = 150;

                        if (plainText.length <= limit) {
                          return plainText;
                        }

                        return `${plainText.substring(0, limit).trimEnd()}...`;
                      })()}
```
